            <div xml:id="d14">

                <pb facs="0031" n="21" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg21"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01 American Military Government/9a:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-21T13:00:00-04:00">January 21, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>512. For your information, the British Embassy has informed the Department that
                    Mr. Strang proposed to bring before the Commission the paper on Civil Affairs in
                    France dated October 6, and desired to <pb facs="0032" n="22" xml:id="pg22"/>
                    suggest at the same time that the Committee adopt a recommendation that the
                    whole question of French Civil Affairs be discussed with the French Committee.
                    The Embassy was informed that we could give no approval to such a
                    recommendation, and it was suggested that the Commission take note of the paper
                    without making any recommendation as to methods of carrying it out.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
